{"task_id": "HumanEval/13", "solution": "def greatest_common_divisor(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" Return a greatest common divisor of two integers a and b\n    >>> greatest_common_divisor(3, 5)\n    1\n    >>> greatest_common_divisor(25, 15)\n    5\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle edge case GCD(0,0) = 0\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Take absolute values as GCD is typically defined for positive integers\n    # and GCD(a,b) = GCD(|a|,|b|)\n    a = abs(a)\n    b = abs(b)\n\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    return a"}
