{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\nclass EmptyListError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised when an operation is performed on an empty list.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message=\"Input list cannot be empty.\"):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\nclass NonNumericTypeError(TypeError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised when a list contains non-numeric types.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message=\"Input list must contain only numeric types (int or float).\"):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        raise EmptyListError()\n\n    for item in l:\n        if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            raise NonNumericTypeError()\n\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # Odd number of elements\n        return sorted_l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        # Even number of elements\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n```\n"}
