{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n. Assume n > 1 and is not a prime.\"\"\"\n    largest_factor = 1\n    d = 2\n    temp_n = n\n\n    while d * d <= temp_n:\n        if temp_n % d == 0:\n            largest_factor = d\n            while temp_n % d == 0:\n                temp_n //= d\n        d += 1\n\n    if temp_n > 1:  # If temp_n is still greater than 1, it is the largest prime factor\n        largest_factor = temp_n\n\n    return largest_factor\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "def derivative(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs represent coefficients of a polynomial.\n    xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[2] * x^2 + ....\n     Return derivative of this polynomial in the same form.\n    >>> derivative([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    [1, 4, 12, 20]\n    >>> derivative([1, 2, 3])\n    [2, 6]\n    \"\"\"\n    if not xs or len(xs) == 1:\n        return []\n\n    derivative_coeffs = []\n    # The derivative of c_i * x^i is i * c_i * x^(i-1).\n    # The new coefficients are generated by iterating from the second original term (index 1).\n    for i in range(1, len(xs)):\n        derivative_coeffs.append(i * xs[i])\n\n    return derivative_coeffs"}
